fpcmoh: fix up the a900's image message for the host matcher

This is what stopped the login working. The image was reaching the host intact
and being rejected before the algorithm ever ran, because the sensor and the
matcher disagree about the image message header by ten bytes.

fpc_enclave_process_data() reassembles one application message across however
many TLS records it takes, and dispatches when it is complete:

    img_len = recv_len - 0xa - 0x18;               /* 34 byte prefix, hardcoded */
    if (img_len != fpc_bep_image_get_size (img))
      return -1;
    ...
    memcpy (pixels, msgbuf + 0x22, img_size);      /* pixel source +34, hardcoded */

The a900 declares total = 11288 for its 64 x 176 sensor: a 24 byte prefix and
11264 pixel bytes. libfpcbep.so wants 34, computes 11288 - 34 = 11254, compares
that against 11264 and returns -1. The driver discarded that return value, so
every sample came back IMAGE_LOW_QUALITY from an algorithm that had never been
handed an image, "remaining" never moved off 16, and enrollment reported eleven
passed stages and stored a template built from nothing.

Nothing else about the blob is wrong for this sensor -- measured against it:

    fpc_hw_get_sensor_details_for_hardware_id(0x331) -> type 7, w 64, h 176
    fpc_enclave_init(enclave, 0x331)                 -> 0
    fpc_bep_image_get_size(image)                    -> 11264 == 64 * 176

and the metadata the enclave reads sits at 0x0c..0x15, inside the first 22 bytes,
so it is correctly placed in both layouts. Only the gap between the metadata and
the pixels differs: the a900 sends two bytes there, the blob expects twelve.

The message is TLS between the sensor's firmware and the blob's own mbedtls, so
the driver cannot change it on the wire. It can move it once it has landed: after
the first record, open a ten byte gap at offset 24 and tell the blob the message
is ten bytes longer. Later records then land correctly by themselves, because the
blob appends at dst + recv_len. What the blob finally sees is the layout it was
built for.

Offsets into libfpcbep.so come from its disassembly and are pinned to the build
installed here (md5 f7136fd774d5208e629bbeaa4974543a). They are checked before
use, not trusted: the TLS state word must read 16, the blob's own destination
pointer must be the buffer we think it is, and the declared length must be
exactly this sensor's image plus 24. If any of that fails this does nothing and
the driver behaves exactly as it did before.

Enabled only for 10a5:a900. The 9800 is untouched.

Not upstreamable, and not offered as such: reaching into another library's
private state is the price of a closed matcher. The clean fixes are a blob built
for this message format, or a sensor that sends the format this blob was built
for. This also fixes a real driver bug on the way -- fpc_enclave_process_data()'s
return value is no longer discarded.

Applies on top of merge request 396 and patches 0001-0006.
